{{also|pull-out|pullout}}
==English==

===Verb===
'''[[pull]] [[out]]''' (of)

# {{idiom}} To [[withdraw]]; especially of [[military]] [[forces]]; to [[retreat]].
#:''The troops '''pulled out''' of the conflict.''
# {{literally}} To use [[coitus interruptus]] as a method of [[birth control]].
# {{idiom}} To [[remove]] something from a container.
#:''He '''pulled out''' his gun before she had a chance to scream.''
# {{idiom}} To [[maneuver]] a vehicle from the side of a road onto the [[lane]].
#:''When joining a road, you should check for traffic before '''pulling out'''.''

====Synonyms====
*{{sense|removing something from a container}} [[whip out]]
 
